    "auto_generated": true,
    "text": "A Bayesian linear regression compared 8 models for mpg (JZS prior scale r = 0.354).\n\nThe best model is 'wt + hp' with posterior probability 0.436, R² = 0.827 and BF₁₀ = 7.89 × 10⁸ against the null model.\n\nInclusion Bayes factors: wt BF = 1.95 × 10⁴; hp BF = 1.23; qsec BF = 1.17.\n\nThe posterior coefficients are slopes in the outcome's units per unit of each predictor (posterior means, which are shrunk towards zero)."
  },
  "notes": [],
  "module": "bayes_regression",
  "module_version": "1.0.0",
  "title": "Bayesian Linear Regression",
  "status": "ok",
  "code": "library(BayesFactor)\nlibrary(bayestestR)\n# Bayesian linear regression: mpg on wt, hp, qsec\nd <- data[complete.cases(data[, c(\"mpg\", \"wt\", \"hp\", \"qsec\")]), c(\"mpg\", \"wt\", \"hp\", \"qsec\")]\nrscale <- sqrt(2) / 4   # JZS prior scale on the standardized coefficients\nbf <- regressionBF(mpg ~ wt + hp + qsec, data = d, rscaleCont = rscale, progress = FALSE)   # every subset of predictors\nx <- extractBF(bf)\nmodels <- data.frame(model = c(\"Null model\", rownames(x)), bf10 = c(1, x$bf), error = c(NA, x$error))\nmodels$p_post <- models$bf10 / sum(models$bf10)   # P(M|data), all models equally likely a priori\nmodels <- models[order(-models$bf10), ]\nmodels$r2 <- sapply(models$model, function(m) if (m == \"Null model\") 0 else\n  summary(lm(paste(\"mpg\", \"~\", m), data = d))$r.squared)\ninclusion <- bayesfactor_inclusion(bf)\n# Posterior coefficients of the best model\nbest <- models$model[1]\nif (best != \"Null model\") {\n  set.seed(123)\n  fit <- lmBF(as.formula(paste(\"mpg\", \"~\", best)), data = d, rscaleCont = rscale)\n  post <- posterior(fit, iterations = 10000, progress = FALSE)\n}",
